              "What is a Chipset?",
              "The chipset is a set of chips (or a single chip in modern systems) on the motherboard that manages data flow between the CPU, memory, storage, and peripherals. Think of it as the traffic management system of the computer. The chipset determines what features the motherboard supports — how many USB ports, which generation of SATA, whether overclocking is possible.",
