    connection: "This week covers the storage layer in detail — how data is physically organized on drives (file systems, partitioning, formatting) and how to recover data when things go wrong. This directly addresses CO-03 (Manage File Systems through formatting, partitioning, data backup and recovery). The skills learned here connect to Week 10 (Networking) where we learn to share files across the network — understanding file systems is prerequisite to setting up shared folders correctly.",
