    previousSummary: "Week 12 covered e-waste management comprehensively: definition and types of e-waste, global generation statistics (62 million tonnes in 2022), toxic substances (lead, mercury, cadmium, BFRs, PVC) and their health/environmental impacts, the three-stage device lifecycle (production, usage, end-of-life), formal recycling processes (collection through refining), and India's regulatory framework (E-Waste Management Rules 2022 with EPR provisions). We now understand how to responsibly manage hardware from purchase to disposal.",
